\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 1951 to 2025 across 8 grids, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years, the same count as May to June. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 24% of normal in August to September and 236% in May to June. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 14869 at 54%. On grid 15168 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 69.1, and that can still change.</p>"}
